```c
fflt_dbg = er32(FFLT_DBG);
fflt_dbg |= E1000_FFLT_DBG_DONT_GATE_WAKE_DMA_CLK;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the DMA clock is gated from the modPHY block during the hardware MAC initialization flow. This improper configuration prevents the necessary clock signal from being available, leading to packet loss when sending packets in burst mode on the Kumeran interface, particularly on Tiger Lake and later platforms.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (mac->type >= e1000_pch_tgp) {
    fflt_dbg = er32(FFLT_DBG);
    fflt_dbg |= E1000_FFLT_DBG_DONT_GATE_WAKE_DMA_CLK;
    ew32(FFLT_DBG, fflt_dbg);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves modifying the hardware MAC initialization flow to ensure that the DMA clock is not gated from the modPHY block. By adding this check and setting the appropriate bit in the FFLT_DBG register, the necessary clock signal is maintained, preventing packet loss during burst mode transmissions.

